A||||7||Dan86gt3.8||Timken bearings suck||||1||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||12-25-2000||01:29 AM||||Well I found out what was making my car jek back and forth  and all over the place and be unstable.  I jaked up the back and went to take off the right wheel to check things and I could move the wheel (i estimate maybe 2 inches back and forth).  I take the wheel of and take of the whell bearing and sure enough there is major play in it.  The bearing moved in and out of the triangular piece that bolts ot the strut or whatever about an inch or so.  But here is the kicker, we replaced the wheel bearing right before I went to school (approx. 4 months ago).  So I take the bearing back to autozone and luckily it only had 90 day warentte on it.  I don't know if I just got  a bad wheel bearing or if they all suck but thats what happened.  Anywyas my car feels great now.  <P>ps- I am abnout to get my mits on a digital camera.  Does anyone wana see pics of a 3.8?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||12-25-2000||01:45 PM||||I'd love to see them!||||reg||10
Z||000002||theogre||12-25-2000||03:52 PM||||sounds like you got a bad set or they were not installed right. I've used Timken for 20+ years and never had a problem with them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-25-2000||04:36 PM||||timken probable make 80% of all bearing, cars, planes anything. Ive never had a prob with them. but like above post says, guess there could be a bad one, or improperly installed, lack of lube.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||12-25-2000||06:50 PM||||Be sure you properly torque the axle nut (200 ft lbs)||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||12-25-2000||11:45 PM||||200 if it's a new nut. Used ones get less. 70 acording to haynes altho I usually go more.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||12-26-2000||01:07 AM||||I have just always used the impact wrench to tighten it down.  I mean I guess I could have got a bad bearing or something but I was just mad it didn't have a very long warante.  So its like 55 for a bearing that we were replacing like 4 months later...  It might have just ben bad luck!<P>ps- I will take pics tomorow<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||12-27-2000||05:34 PM||||Just put those Timken bearings on my formula in September ($50 each). Both the factory units were shot because the previous owner drove the car with the e-brake on and cooked them along with the rear brakes too. The car only had 50k on it. There was allot of slop in them. Those things must have been red hot to do that much damage. ||||reg||1
